      "date": "2026-10-13 18:10:35.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(3 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good; the option parsing, the /proc/mounts and sbi_flags output, and the SB_I_CGROUPWB gating all look correct. The nits inline are optional and can wait for the next refresh; no need to re-spin for them. Also, if the patch is refreshed: usage() in lustre/utils/mount_lustre.c lists the other client (no)xxx options such as (no)checksum, (no)lruresize and (no)lazystatfs. Should it list \"(no)cgroupwb: disable or enable* cgroup writeback\" too, so that `mount.lustre --help` shows the new option?",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
