          "email": "jinshanx@google.com",
          "date": "2026-10-12 19:00:32.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20936 llite: add nocgroupwb mount option",
        "message": "LU-20936 llite: add nocgroupwb mount option\n\nLustre clients always set SB_I_CGROUPWB on the superblock, so every\ninode a cgroup dirties is attached to that cgroup's writeback\ncontext. When the cgroup is removed, for example when a container\nexits, the kernel has to switch all of those inodes back to a parent\nwriteback context in inode_switch_wbs_work_fn(). On clients with a\nvery large inode cache this produces a large number of CPU-hogging\nwork items contending on wb->list_lock, which can stall kernel\nworkqueues for minutes. The client stops pinging during the stall\nand gets evicted. Newer kernels (v6.18) make the switching cheaper,\nbut on older kernels Lustre gives no way to opt out.\n\nAdd client mount options \"cgroupwb\" and \"nocgroupwb\", backed by the\nnew LL_SBI_CGROUPWB flag. \"cgroupwb\" is the default and keeps the\ncurrent behaviour. \"nocgroupwb\" makes ll_fill_super() skip setting\nSB_I_CGROUPWB, so inodes stay on the bdi root writeback context and\nare never switched between cgroup writeback contexts. The trade-off\nis that dirty throttling and reclaim writeback become system-wide\nrather than per cgroup (see LU-16713). The option takes effect at\nmount time only.\n\nDocument both options in mount.lustre.8.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Jinshan Xiong <jinshanx@google.com>\nChange-Id: I5e450c4be95c1bc048409e6050fecf6ed185e442\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
